> Expanding the selected pair's right triangle

For the ideal decimal coordinates, Δx=0.03 and Δy=−0.02, so
d=√(0.03²+0.02²)=√0.0013≈0.036055512755. Stored double coordinates are
rounded decimal inputs; the program prints their actual widened differences.
The equal-scale native diagram expands only the selected pair and its two
orthogonal coordinate differences. Marker radii are presentation choices,
not physical disks or search thresholds.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/closest_pair_zoom.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto points=dm::geometry::uniform_rectangle_points(60,424242);
  points.push_back({5,5});points.push_back({5.03,4.98});
  const auto result=dm::geometry::closest_pair_indexed(points);const auto a=result.a,b=result.b;
  const long double dx=static_cast<long double>(b.x)-a.x,dy=static_cast<long double>(b.y)-a.y;
  std::print("| measured quantity | actual value |\n| :--- | ---: |\n| delta x | {:.18g} |\n| delta y | {:.18g} |\n| widened distance | {:.18g} |\n",dx,dy,result.distance);
  dm::graphics::Diagram figure(10000,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke legs;legs.dashed=true;legs.color={100,116,139};legs.width=1.5;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke diagonal;diagonal.color={220,38,38};diagonal.width=2.5;
  figure.path({{a.x,a.y},{b.x,a.y},{b.x,b.y}},legs)
        .path({{a.x,a.y},{b.x,b.y}},diagonal)
        .ellipse({a.x,a.y},0.0004,0.0004,{220,38,38})
        .ellipse({b.x,b.y},0.0004,0.0004,{220,38,38})
        .text({a.x-0.003,a.y+0.006},std::format("index {}: (5,5)",result.first),20)
        .text({b.x+0.005,b.y-0.005},std::format("index {}: (5.03,4.98)",result.second),20)
        .text({5.015,5.003},std::format("dx={:.2f}",dx),20)
        .text({5.040,4.990},std::format("dy={:.2f}",dy),20)
        .text({5.015,5.015},"The selected pair at equal coordinate scale",23)
        .text({5.015,4.965},std::format("measured separation {:.12f}",result.distance),21)
        .save_svg("build/closest_pair_zoom.svg");
}
