> Work grows with pairs, not improvement records

The exact unordered-pair count is

$$
C(n)=\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}(n-i-1)=\frac{n(n-1)}{2}.
$$
\alttext(The nested scan visits n times n minus one divided by two unordered pairs.)

The kernel evaluates every pair, including after a zero distance is found.
Ordinary indexed search uses O(1) auxiliary storage and Θ(n²) distance work.
A trace adds O(K) owned records for K strict improvements, with K≤C(n).
An often-small observed K does not reduce the number of distance evaluations
or establish a subquadratic bound. On doubling input size,
C(2n)/C(n)=4+2/(n−1), tending to four.

The next plot compares actual counted distance evaluations to the exact
formula. These are logical operations, not timings or empirical speedups.
Faster planar divide-and-conquer algorithms use a maintained y-order and a
bounded-neighbour strip merge to achieve O(n log n); that is background, not
the algorithm or a performance promise of this all-pairs API.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/closest_pair_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> size,measured,formula;
  std::print("| points n | actual pair visits | n(n-1)/2 | actual improvements |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n=8;n<=512;n*=2) {
    const auto points=dm::geometry::uniform_rectangle_points(n,424242);
    const auto trace=dm::geometry::closest_pair_trace(points);const auto expected=n*(n-1)/2;
    if(trace.work.pair_visits!=expected)return 1;
    size.push_back(n);measured.push_back(trace.work.distance_evaluations);formula.push_back(expected);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,trace.work.pair_visits,expected,trace.improvements.size());
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(size,formula,"formula",{234,88,12},1.8)
      .points(size,measured,"actual",{37,99,235},5)
      .legend({"n(n-1)/2","native visits"},{{234,88,12},{37,99,235}})
      .title("Actual all-pairs work follows the exact pair count")
      .x_label("input point records").y_label("distance evaluations")
      .x_limits(0,530).y_limits(0,145000).save_svg("build/closest_pair_work.svg");
}
```
